              "type": "text",
              "content": "Curiosity | Textbook of Science | Grade 6"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.084,
            0.893,
            0.111,
            0.908
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "26"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.084,
            0.886,
            0.261
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In deserts, food is not available easily. Camels store food in their humps. Camels found in the hot desert have one hump each that helps them to survive during the scarcity of food. Camels found in the cold desert have two humps each. These two humps shrink in late winters because there is not much food available in the cold desert and they have to use food stored in their humps during that time. Moreover, they grow long hair from head to neck, which help them survive the cold winters of Ladakh."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.262,
            0.883,
            0.301
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What other features can help camels to survive in the desert?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.302,
            0.885,
            0.401
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Other students also start sharing their observations. Kashi from Rajasthan says that camels excrete small amounts of urine, their dung is dry, and they do not sweat. As camels do not lose much water from their bodies, they can survive for many days without drinking water."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.401,
            0.885,
            0.58
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Maya talks about seeing plants with beautiful bright flowers, "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "rhododendrons",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", in the Shola forests of Nilgiris. Here, rhododendrons are of shorter height and have smaller leaves to survive through the heavy winds on mountain tops. However, Pema, who is from Sikkim, mentions that she has observed rhododendrons in the nearby mountains to be taller (Fig. 2.13). So, even plants such as rhododendrons may exhibit different features in different regions to survive the conditions of those regions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.404,
            0.592,
            0.73,
            0.779
          ],
          "content": [
